course: dictionary
lesson: 12603
title: Disconnected: cut off or jumbled
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Disconnected» is a word with three meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. When something is not plugged in or linked to power or the internet, it is disconnected. «The tablet was disconnected from the Wi-Fi, so the video would not play.» The Wi-Fi clue tells you it means cut off from the internet.
explain: «His ideas were disconnected, jumping from football to pizza and back.» Here the word is about thoughts, not machines. The ideas do not follow on from each other, so disconnected means jumbled. Always ask: does the sentence mean a thing, a set of thoughts, or a feeling about people?
explain: «Since moving house, Sam has felt disconnected from his old friends.» This is about feelings. Sam is not in trouble with his phone; he feels cut off and lonely. Try swapping in your meaning. Does «felt cut off from his old friends» still make sense? Then you have it.
fact: «Disconnected» means not connected or plugged in, or cut off from a power supply or network.
fact: «Disconnected» can also describe ideas or speech that do not follow on clearly; they are jumbled.
fact: Feeling disconnected means feeling cut off from other people, lonely, or as if you do not belong.
fact: «Disconnected» is also the past form of the verb «disconnect», as in «The man disconnected the hose.»
fact: Useful phrases: «disconnected from», «feel disconnected», and «disconnected thoughts».
exercise: «The tablet was disconnected from the Wi-Fi, so the video would not play.» What does disconnected mean here? | Loud and noisy | Made of wood | Very happy and excited | *Not plugged in or linked to the internet
exercise: «His ideas were disconnected, jumping from football to pizza and back.» What does disconnected suggest? | Written in a neat list | Very long and detailed | *Jumbled, with no clear link between the ideas | Clear and easy to follow
exercise: «Since moving house, Sam has felt disconnected from his old friends.» Which feeling does this show? | Proud of his new bike | Full of energy | Bored of school dinners | *Cut off and lonely
test: Which word is closest in meaning to disconnected? | Joined | *Cut off | Bright | Hungry
test: The writer says, «The story felt disconnected, with scenes that did not join up.» What does the writer mean? | Full of pictures | Happy and cheerful | Very quick and exciting | *The parts did not link together clearly
exam: «After the power cut, the lamp stayed disconnected until the electrician came.» What does disconnected mean? | *Not supplied with power, cut off from electricity | Dropped on the floor | Made of glass | Switched on and bright
